### Eureka Server - example requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Run the Eureka Server first. Dashboard in browser: http://localhost:8761

@eureka = http://localhost:8762

### 1. Health check - expect {"status":"UP", ...}
GET {{eureka}}/actuator/health

### 2. Application info - expect the name and description from application.yml
GET {{eureka}}/actuator/info

### 3. All registered applications (JSON)
# Right now: an empty "application" list.
# After later phases: API-GATEWAY, PRODUCT-SERVICE, MCP-SERVER, MCP-CLIENT.
GET {{eureka}}/eureka/apps
Accept: application/json

### 4. One application by name (works after Phase 2 starts product-service)
# Eureka stores application names in UPPERCASE.
# Expect 404 until product-service is running.
GET {{eureka}}/eureka/apps/PRODUCT-SERVICE
Accept: application/json
